      {
        "line": 36,
        "text": "        This class composes forces and torques applied to rigid bodies. Forces and torques can be"
      },
      {
        "line": 37,
        "text": "        specified in either the global (world) frame or the local (body) frame. Internally, they are"
      },
      {
        "line": 38,
        "text": "        stored in separate global and local input buffers. When the final composed wrench is needed,"
      },
      {
        "line": 39,
        "text": "        the global contributions are rotated into the body frame and combined with the local"
      },
      {
        "line": 40,
        "text": "        contributions to produce the output force and torque expressed in the body frame."
      },
      {
        "line": 44,
        "text": "        - ``global_force_w``: Global forces [N] (world frame)."
      },
      {
        "line": 45,
        "text": "        - ``global_torque_w``: Global torques [N\u00b7m] (world frame), including moment contributions"
      },
      {
        "line": 46,
        "text": "          from positional forces (``cross(P, F)``)."
      },
      {
        "line": 47,
        "text": "        - ``global_force_at_com_w``: Global forces [N] applied at the body's CoM (world frame, no positional torque)."
      },
      {
        "line": 48,
        "text": "        - ``local_force_b``: Local forces [N] (body frame)."
      },
      {
        "line": 49,
        "text": "        - ``local_torque_b``: Local torques [N\u00b7m] (body frame)."
      },
      {
        "line": 53,
        "text": "        - ``out_force_b``: Composed force [N] in body frame."
      },
      {
        "line": 54,
        "text": "        - ``out_torque_b``: Composed torque [N\u00b7m] in body frame."
      },
      {
        "line": 79,
